1
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:35,039
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:37,690
[Episode 22]

3
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:39,640
Next week,

4
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,560
Bolly is holding

5
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:42,070
a distributor investment event.

6
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:43,470
Are you interested in it?

7
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:43,950
But whether

8
00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:45,170
you can get the distributorship

9
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:46,229
all depends on you.

10
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,650
The mere distributorship?

11
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,250
I'll get it for sure.

12
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:54,530
Here we are.

13
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:56,000
Here you go, sir.

14
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:56,680
Alright.

15
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:07,570
The fare is 20 yuan.

16
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,610
You're 10 short.

17
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,150
I'm not short. You took a detour.

18
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:12,800
How dare you ask for more money then?

19
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,600
That's a one-way street!
We couldn't get through!

20
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:16,630
Stop trying to fool me.

21
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:17,680
One-way street? Seriously?

22
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,560
I get my goods from there every day.

23
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,560
You think I don't know?

24
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:19,890
Um...

25
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:21,579
Cut the crap. It's on the meter.

26
00:02:21,579 --> 00:02:23,110
You took a detour. I paid...

27
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:23,950
How much is it?

28
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,430
Ten yuan!

29
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:28,920
Don't... Don't pay him.

30
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:29,850
He took a detour.

31
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:31,670
There's no time to lose.

32
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:34,520
Well,

33
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:36,400
here, 10 yuan for you.

34
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:38,910
I was not trying to rip him off.

35
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:40,040
But he took a detour.

36
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:41,280
He called

37
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,079
Pingchuan Alley a one-way street.

38
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:44,400
But it's not.

39
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,230
He just took a detour.

40
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:48,890
We're going to be late.

41
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:19,360
So many people.

42
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,520
By the time we finish signing in,
it'll be too late.

43
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:35,280
This way.

44
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:40,480
Hi, Manager.

45
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,040
You're

46
00:04:46,210 --> 00:04:47,360
such a big shot here?

47
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:48,590
She was greeting you.

48
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:52,000
What on earth

49
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,270
is on your mind all day?

50
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,500
Didn't I tell you that?

51
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,960
I just got promoted
to regional operations manager.

52
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,440
I'm a manager, after all.

53
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:00,190
Hello, Manager.

54
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:00,590
Hello.

55
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,680
Impressive.

56
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,870
I'm in awe.

57
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,520
It's in there.

58
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:21,550
Once you go in,

59
00:05:21,950 --> 00:05:23,010
you're on your own.

60
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,120
Give me the umbrella.

61
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,010
Go ahead.

62
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,120
Hello, Ms. Qi.

63
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:59,040
I've reviewed your application form.

64
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,890
The financial proof section

65
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:01,800
is blank.

66
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:03,360
If you become a distributor,

67
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,650
you'll need to pay Bolly

68
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:06,800
a certain deposit

69
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,120
and advance payment.

70
00:06:08,190 --> 00:06:09,480
Could you provide

71
00:06:09,510 --> 00:06:10,720
your bank statements?

72
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,870
Either corporate
or personal ones will do.

73
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:14,120
It doesn't need to be much.

74
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,070
A continuous balance

75
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:16,180
of over 2 million for 6 months

76
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:16,780
is enough.

77
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:21,750
I...

78
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:25,470
I don't have it with me today.

79
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:27,000
Can I bring it next time?

80
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:30,480
That's fine.

81
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:31,430
Ms. Qi,

82
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:32,570
how many people

83
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,130
are currently in your team?

84
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:35,870
Twenty.

85
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,390
Well, here's the case, Ms. Qi.

86
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:38,159
Our team

87
00:06:38,190 --> 00:06:40,120
mainly targets mid-to-high-end customers.

88
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,270
The store requires

89
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,600
professionals in market research,

90
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,480
sales,

91
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,620
customer service,

92
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,920
inventory management,

93
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,630
and so on.

94
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:48,920
Your team

95
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,390
of 20 people

96
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,050
might not be enough.

97
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:53,040
Also, Ms. Qi,

98
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,010
may I ask

99
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:55,480
about the sales revenue

100
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,120
of your team?

101
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,780
What's your annual turnover?

102
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,520
You mean 10 million?

103
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,270
Here's the thing.

104
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,790
If we don't have enough staff,
we can hire more.

105
00:07:23,050 --> 00:07:24,160
The sales revenue isn't high,

106
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:24,600
but...

107
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:25,720
But we're

108
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,120
all highly skilled

109
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:27,980
salespersons.

110
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,170
If

111
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:30,870
Bolly gives us a chance,

112
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,510
we might deliver results

113
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,570
that exceed expectations.

114
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:42,390
Bolly can make

115
00:07:44,390 --> 00:07:45,190
any requests.

116
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,320
We will fully cooperate.

117
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,040
Then tell us about

118
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:51,870
your takes
on Bolly's future brand enhancement

119
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:53,370
and the expansion

120
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,680
of overseas markets.

121
00:07:58,830 --> 00:07:59,630
Enhancement?

122
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:06,160
As for overseas markets...

123
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:08,530
I...

124
00:08:08,950 --> 00:08:09,560
I...

125
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,630
Or,

126
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:15,950
let's say you've already opened a store.

127
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:16,390
How do you

128
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:17,450
plan to make sales?

129
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,560
Just briefly walk us through

130
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,490
your sales plan.

131
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,240
Sales plan...

132
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:30,280
Or you can think about it...

133
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:46,440
Production process.

134
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,840
Improve efficiency and quality

135
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,360
and reduce costs.

136
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,530
Well, how about you

137
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,200
redo that data chart?

138
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:52,500
Got it, Manager.

139
00:08:55,510 --> 00:08:56,240
How did it go?

140
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,460
Did you do this on purpose?

141
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:13,430
What's wrong?

142
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:17,750
Your company sets such a high bar.

143
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:18,510
Why didn't you

144
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:19,570
make it clear to me?

145
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,790
And you said stores of all sizes

146
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:23,050
were welcome to apply.

147
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,240
You know

148
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,690
I'm not even qualified to walk

149
00:09:26,690 --> 00:09:27,750
into your company.

150
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:30,080
I was a total joke in there.

151
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:32,270
Wait,

152
00:09:32,270 --> 00:09:33,470
what did they ask you?

153
00:09:33,870 --> 00:09:35,440
Is there any misunderstanding?

154
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,170
Manager Cao.

155
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,240
Here's a document

156
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,970
that needs Mr. Li's signature.

157
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:41,530
Okay.

158
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:42,720
I'll have him sign it

159
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,720
when he returns this afternoon.

160
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,050
Okay.

161
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:47,600
So,

162
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,550
it's our first year

163
00:09:48,550 --> 00:09:49,000
carrying out

164
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
the regional investment
and ordering system.

165
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,600
But I'm not the one in charge

166
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:53,690
of the investment.

167
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:54,630
So I'm also not so sure

168
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:55,550
what qualification questions

169
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:56,610
they've prepared.

170
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:00,840
If their questions

171
00:10:00,870 --> 00:10:01,910
upset you,

172
00:10:03,030 --> 00:10:04,630
I apologize on their behalf.

173
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:05,960
But don't give up.

174
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:07,240
There might be

175
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,870
other chances for cooperation.

176
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:09,360
Cao Xin.

177
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:14,070
Just a moment.

178
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:17,680
Mr. Zhang.

179
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:19,430
Double-check

180
00:10:19,430 --> 00:10:20,630
the decimal points

181
00:10:19,450 --> 00:10:23,410
♪ The wind blew through our hair ♪

182
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,930
in the document.

183
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:25,900
Make sure the clients review
the materials in advance.

184
00:10:26,070 --> 00:10:29,740
♪ The story slowly gets complicated too ♪

185
00:10:32,730 --> 00:10:37,740
♪ We never became anyone's myth ♪

186
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,200
I'll get on it now.

187
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:36,530
Okay.

188
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:43,740
♪ We only learned to grow up in the rain ♪

189
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:44,390
I'll come get it later.

190
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:44,750
Okay.

191
00:10:46,390 --> 00:10:49,990
♪ Should we blame fate? ♪

192
00:10:52,270 --> 00:10:56,320
♪ Adulthood is bandaging your own falls ♪

193
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:57,970
You forgot your umbrella.

194
00:10:58,390 --> 00:10:58,870
Thanks.

195
00:10:59,150 --> 00:11:02,190
♪ Rented rooms, the last bus home ♪

196
00:11:02,030 --> 00:11:03,030
Let me treat you to lunch.

197
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:04,440
♪ What does the future hold? ♪

198
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,270
There's a Cantonese restaurant

199
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:09,730
♪ It's been so long since I last
dared to say I was afraid ♪

200
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,600
near our company.

201
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:13,220
The restaurant near your company

202
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:16,600
♪ Though we have nothing,
we still bustle about ♪

203
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,570
must be expensive, huh?

204
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,310
Like 300 to 400 yuan per person?

205
00:11:19,310 --> 00:11:23,610
♪ Because the answer is clear
as long as you are around ♪

206
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:21,920
I can't afford that.

207
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:23,320
I'm out.

208
00:11:25,030 --> 00:11:25,690
Don't be stubborn.

209
00:11:25,690 --> 00:11:27,790
♪ The old dreams are now covered in dust ♪

210
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:30,270
♪ But it's okay ♪

211
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,840
If things didn't go smoothly,

212
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,170
let me go over it with you

213
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:32,600
and see what the problem is.

214
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:37,900
♪ The morning glow will finally appear ♪

215
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,080
What problem?

216
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:39,240
It's my problem!

217
00:11:40,550 --> 00:11:41,270
From start to end,

218
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:43,130
it's just that I don't deserve it.

219
00:11:55,030 --> 00:11:55,890
What happened?

220
00:11:59,270 --> 00:12:00,270
You're barefoot!

221
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:05,910
Be careful!

222
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:10,510
♪ Who hasn't panicked
in this fast-paced world? ♪

223
00:12:10,550 --> 00:12:11,200
Shoes!

224
00:12:12,510 --> 00:12:13,440
You're barefoot!

225
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:19,050
♪ All I see is your gaze ♪

226
00:12:19,710 --> 00:12:24,300
♪ If there's nothing left tomorrow ♪

227
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,240
Sir, sir,

228
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:24,910
you can just

229
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:25,970
pull over up ahead.

230
00:12:26,510 --> 00:12:27,270
This is a no-parking zone.

231
00:12:26,530 --> 00:12:37,210
♪ I'll still walk you home ♪

232
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:29,120
Let me go a bit further to pull over.

233
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:29,910
This isn't a no-parking zone.

234
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:30,510
I live around here.

235
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:31,670
Would I not know
if it's a no-parking zone?

236
00:12:31,670 --> 00:12:32,750
Just pull over right there.

237
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:33,150
Miss,

238
00:12:33,550 --> 00:12:34,410
I really can't.

239
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,600
I'm the one who gets fined,

240
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,200
not you.

241
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,440
I'll go a bit further

242
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,970
and stop around the corner.

243
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,140
Around the corner?

244
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,680
Alright, here we are.

245
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,120
You have arrived at your destination.

246
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,320
Please pay the amount

247
00:12:49,390 --> 00:12:50,600
shown on the meter.

248
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,320
Make sure
you take your belongings with you.

249
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,520
Alright, be careful.

250
00:12:58,630 --> 00:12:59,080
Miss,

251
00:12:59,690 --> 00:13:00,550
I didn't do anything to you!

252
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:01,790
What's with the bad attitude?

253
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,480
Keep that up,
and you'll never get a boyfriend.

254
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,980
Who wants a boyfriend?

255
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,030
I want money!

256
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,170
You're back.

257
00:13:18,870 --> 00:13:20,820
Why did you come back barefoot?

258
00:13:22,270 --> 00:13:23,080
I went through all the trouble

259
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:25,310
to attend a distributor investment event,

260
00:13:25,310 --> 00:13:27,510
only to be mocked
both openly and secretly.

261
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:28,440
What a lousy day!

262
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,440
You look so mad.

263
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:32,790
Given our capabilities,

264
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:35,870
do we even need to attend
the investment event?

265
00:13:37,030 --> 00:13:38,690
Were it not for that nuisance,

266
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:39,990
I wouldn't have gone!

267
00:13:40,670 --> 00:13:41,600
I even took a cab.

268
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,120
The round trip

269
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,950
wasted me 30 yuan.

270
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:48,810
We're just not making enough.

271
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:50,240
I watched the store for you today

272
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:50,960
and didn't sell

273
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,560
a single piece this morning.

274
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:54,410
A few customers came in later,

275
00:13:54,510 --> 00:13:56,000
but they just kept trying on the clothes.

276
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
It exhausted me.

277
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:57,960
I thought

278
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,720
I could at least sell a few.

279
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,750
Hasn't it just been like this lately?

280
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,410
Trying on clothes without buying.

281
00:14:04,410 --> 00:14:05,600
Why would they waste time

282
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,260
doing that?

283
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,930
I heard them whispering that

284
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:10,670
it was cheaper to buy and easier

285
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:11,670
to return online.

286
00:14:11,910 --> 00:14:12,710
They probably

287
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,390
came here just to try them on

288
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:16,050
and will buy them online then.

289
00:14:17,630 --> 00:14:19,120
But my prices are also not high.

290
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,360
And I accept returns, too.

291
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,550
But they still have to make

292
00:14:21,550 --> 00:14:23,080
a trip back here to return them.

293
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:23,880
You know what?

294
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,840
Young people these days

295
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,140
are all lazybones.

296
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:28,510
They just do whatever takes

297
00:14:28,510 --> 00:14:29,510
the least effort.

298
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:30,930
I bet eventually,

299
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,200
they won't even bother coming

300
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,320
to try clothes on.

301
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:35,000
They will

302
00:14:35,270 --> 00:14:37,730
do everything online without leaving home.

303
00:14:40,030 --> 00:14:40,690
Exactly...

304
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,810
If it can be done online,

305
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,490
why not do it online?

306
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:05,940
Come on,

307
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,630
let me propose another toast

308
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:08,790
to our friendship!

309
00:15:08,790 --> 00:15:09,320
Cheers!

310
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:09,780
Cheers!

311
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:10,780
Tianji,

312
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:11,360
use

313
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:12,480
the pitcher.

314
00:15:12,550 --> 00:15:14,000
Come on, I'm a lightweight.

315
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:14,750
Don't...

316
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:16,010
Cheers.

317
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,910
What have you been up to lately?

318
00:15:24,910 --> 00:15:25,440
Come on, eat up.

319
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:26,550
Playing video games.

320
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:27,850
Come on, my old classmate.

321
00:15:27,850 --> 00:15:28,450
Let's

322
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:29,270
have a drink.

323
00:15:30,510 --> 00:15:31,270
Aren't you the one

324
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:33,670
who played a role
in the "Flower Fairy" back then? Wang...

325
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:34,200
Yep...

326
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:34,840
Wang Xiaoyong.

327
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,320
Yes, I'm Wang Xiaoyong.

328
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:37,790
Wang Xiaoyong from Class 8.

329
00:15:37,790 --> 00:15:38,270
Long time no see.

330
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,200
Long time no see.

331
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:46,390
We really should

332
00:15:46,390 --> 00:15:47,390
have the girls from back then

333
00:15:47,390 --> 00:15:48,120
come and see.

334
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,100
The prince has turned into a toad.

335
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,540
They just called him a toad back then.

336
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,130
Have you heard that?

337
00:15:55,410 --> 00:15:56,170
Cao Xin is now

338
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:58,000
the boss of Bolly Fashion Group.

339
00:15:58,150 --> 00:15:59,120
Cao Xin is a boss now?

340
00:15:59,120 --> 00:15:59,850
Impressive!

341
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:00,670
No, that's not true.

342
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:02,360
I'm just an operations manager

343
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,960
in charge
of the group's regional operations.

344
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,080
No matter what, you're still

345
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,360
some sort of an executive, right?

346
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,390
-Yeah.
-Exactly.

347
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:10,010
In just 2 years, Cao Xin

348
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:10,870
went straight

349
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:12,670
from assistant to an executive.

350
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:13,630
I always knew

351
00:16:13,630 --> 00:16:14,560
you had it in you.

352
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,510
Out of all our classes,

353
00:16:15,510 --> 00:16:17,040
I knew you'd make your mark.

354
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,360
As for Qi Shi,

355
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,200
she hasn't amounted to much.

356
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:22,000
Don't even bring her up.

357
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,450
What's wrong with Qi Shi?

358
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:26,640
Wasn't Qi Shi

359
00:16:26,670 --> 00:16:28,070
on par with you in school?

360
00:16:28,270 --> 00:16:28,880
But now,

361
00:16:28,910 --> 00:16:30,150
she can only sell clothes

362
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:31,080
at a street stall

363
00:16:31,390 --> 00:16:31,960
and support

364
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,390
her brother, who got out of jail.

365
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:35,000
Her whole family is dirt-poor now.

366
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:35,480
Yeah...

367
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:36,730
Their family

368
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:38,440
is indeed drowning in debt.

369
00:16:38,550 --> 00:16:39,030
Indeed.

370
00:16:39,510 --> 00:16:40,920
I didn't even dare to say hi
when I ran into her

371
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:42,030
on the street last time.

372
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:44,360
I was afraid
she'd ask me to lend her money.

373
00:16:44,770 --> 00:16:45,840
I just saw her on the overpass

374
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,600
the other day.

375
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:47,270
At her stall, right?

376
00:16:47,270 --> 00:16:47,670
Yeah.

377
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,030
Didn't I just say that

378
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:50,120
studying was useless?

379
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:50,650
Exactly.

380
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,270
What's up?

381
00:16:54,670 --> 00:16:56,200
What is wrong with you guys?

382
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,390
Qi Shi sets up a stall

383
00:16:58,390 --> 00:16:59,440
and sells clothes to earn her living.

384
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,320
What's wrong with that?

385
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,120
Does that make her any inferior?

386
00:17:02,530 --> 00:17:03,010
Besides,

387
00:17:03,010 --> 00:17:05,200
did the Qis ever ask you
to lend them money?

388
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:05,829
Did they?

389
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,329
And look at you guys!

390
00:17:09,589 --> 00:17:10,160
Back in school,

391
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,510
you copied Qi Shi's homework

392
00:17:11,510 --> 00:17:13,000
and sucked up to her every day!

393
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Now you're talking behind her back.

394
00:17:17,069 --> 00:17:17,829
Listen,

395
00:17:18,270 --> 00:17:19,530
we're all classmates.

396
00:17:20,069 --> 00:17:21,510
If you can't have any empathy,

397
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:23,240
at least have some conscience!

398
00:17:24,030 --> 00:17:25,160
Hey, what's wrong with Cao Xin?

399
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:27,490
I think there's something wrong with you!

400
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:28,210
Well...

401
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:41,550
Mom.

402
00:17:45,490 --> 00:17:46,820
This month's allowance

403
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:47,700
for you.

404
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,720
They say children you raise
will look out for you when you're old.

405
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,320
I guess this is what it means.

406
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,960
We are lucky.

407
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:03,020
Yes, of course.

408
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,830
If I remember correctly,

409
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:10,030
we have two kids, huh?

410
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:16,720
Mom,

411
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:19,960
my store just got quite a lot of clothes

412
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:21,350
for middle-aged and elderly people.

413
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:23,880
You can pick whatever you like
when you visit.

414
00:18:25,130 --> 00:18:26,280
I'm not old yet.

415
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:27,790
Who wants
those middle-aged and elderly styles?

416
00:18:27,790 --> 00:18:28,400
I quite like

417
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,740
the dress for young people

418
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:30,760
you picked

419
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:31,960
for me last time.

420
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:33,510
Fine.

421
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,350
You can still pick whatever you like.

422
00:18:35,350 --> 00:18:37,350
They're just sitting there anyway.

423
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,480
Well,

424
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:46,550
you said you were going to attend

425
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:48,270
some investment event last time.

426
00:18:48,270 --> 00:18:50,400
Just the one Cao Xin introduced to you.

427
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,170
How did it go?

428
00:18:51,590 --> 00:18:52,240
How was it?

429
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,540
It was so unreliable, as he was the one

430
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,010
who introduced it to me.

431
00:19:00,030 --> 00:19:01,290
They are a big company.

432
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,900
We are out of their league.

433
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:09,570
But Mom, Dad, don't worry.

434
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,070
I've already figured out a way.

435
00:19:12,070 --> 00:19:13,110
I don't need big companies

436
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,110
or big brands to help.

437
00:19:14,110 --> 00:19:16,240
Our little store can make it on our own.

438
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:19,830
What way?

439
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,440
It's a secret.

440
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:28,110
Miss,

441
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:29,500
could you please fill out a questionnaire?

442
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,200
I'm doing a survey for my clothing store.

443
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:31,660
Miss,

444
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,400
could you please fill out a questionnaire?

445
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:33,830
Hello,

446
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:34,790
could you...

447
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:35,240
No.

448
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:36,440
Excuse me, miss,

449
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,200
could you please fill out a questionnaire?

450
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,130
Thank you, miss.

451
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:40,580
Have a nice day.

452
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,370
Is what our daughter

453
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,510
is doing really going to work?

454
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:46,050
She hasn't

455
00:19:46,050 --> 00:19:47,900
given out many all morning.

456
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:48,970
No worries.

457
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:50,760
Our daughter

458
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:52,120
has a head for business.

459
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:53,810
Didn't she say that?

460
00:19:53,930 --> 00:19:55,380
She needs to do market research first

461
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:57,240
before she makes steady strides.

462
00:19:59,160 --> 00:19:59,550
Miss,

463
00:19:59,830 --> 00:20:00,750
could you fill out a questionnaire?

464
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,960
I don't want the pancake.

465
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,790
I'm going there for buns

466
00:20:02,790 --> 00:20:04,000
with marinated leaf mustard filling.

467
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,400
Their buns are delicious.

468
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:06,860
Are they really that good?

469
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,350
Yeah.

470
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:09,160
You'll want more after you eat some.

471
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,760
Want more after you eat some?

472
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,680
Could they have

473
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:13,740
added something suspicious to them?

474
00:20:13,790 --> 00:20:14,200
No.

475
00:20:15,030 --> 00:20:15,960
They're so good.

476
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:26,360
I'm heading out for a bit.

477
00:20:36,830 --> 00:20:37,440
Oh, God!

478
00:20:38,110 --> 00:20:39,270
Which jerk did this?

479
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:40,640
Who did this?

480
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:50,520
I'll deliver them
to the construction site later.

481
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,400
The workers there are impatient

482
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,440
and blunt.

483
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:55,010
You can't handle them.

484
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:55,680
Okay.

485
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:57,240
Save a portion

486
00:20:57,270 --> 00:20:58,270
for our daughter.

487
00:20:58,350 --> 00:20:59,170
I already did.

488
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:00,800
They're all in this foam box.

489
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:02,650
Call them over

490
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:03,680
to eat later.

491
00:21:11,790 --> 00:21:13,160
Ride carefully on your way.

492
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:13,890
Take it slow.

493
00:21:13,990 --> 00:21:15,120
Okay, I got it.

494
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:19,750
Are you sure you're okay?

495
00:21:19,790 --> 00:21:20,480
Yeah!

496
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:37,610
Big buns!

497
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,720
Big buns for sale!

498
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:41,460
Steaming hot big buns!

499
00:21:50,270 --> 00:21:50,880
Sir.

500
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,050
How many do you want?

501
00:21:53,070 --> 00:21:55,400
Two with marinated leaf mustard filling.

502
00:21:56,110 --> 00:21:57,370
Sweetie, you're done?

503
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,770
Go sit there and eat.

504
00:21:58,880 --> 00:21:59,830
Your mom just left

505
00:21:59,830 --> 00:22:01,360
and saved a portion for you.

506
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:04,660
Business must be good.

507
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:07,480
I wouldn't have any
if you didn't save some for me.

508
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,330
Come on, eat them while they're still hot.

509
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:24,600
It's okay.

510
00:22:25,110 --> 00:22:27,460
Why did you get so many cuts?

511
00:22:28,550 --> 00:22:29,440
It's nothing.

512
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:32,040
It's much easier

513
00:22:32,070 --> 00:22:33,070
than mining coal.

514
00:22:33,270 --> 00:22:34,270
I'm happy with it.

515
00:22:38,030 --> 00:22:40,830
You really know how
to make the best of a bad situation.

516
00:22:40,830 --> 00:22:42,160
And you know what?

517
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:44,510
Don't underestimate our little stall

518
00:22:44,510 --> 00:22:45,680
or

519
00:22:45,790 --> 00:22:46,650
our small cart.

520
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,140
It may be a small business,

521
00:22:51,790 --> 00:22:53,450
but we make pretty good money.

522
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,110
Really.

523
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:58,350
Dad,

524
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,400
I'm your daughter.

525
00:23:02,070 --> 00:23:02,510
You...

526
00:23:03,510 --> 00:23:05,040
You don't have to brag to me.

527
00:23:05,830 --> 00:23:07,270
Why would I brag to you?

528
00:23:08,070 --> 00:23:09,640
Why would I brag to my daughter?

529
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:10,440
You know what?

530
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,040
We may have few customers

531
00:23:12,310 --> 00:23:12,960
right now,

532
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,680
but those in the neighborhood,

533
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:16,210
at that construction site,

534
00:23:16,590 --> 00:23:17,070
and

535
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:18,530
in those office buildings

536
00:23:18,590 --> 00:23:19,590
all call

537
00:23:19,790 --> 00:23:21,350
to order buns at mealtime.

538
00:23:22,070 --> 00:23:23,830
Your mom and I take turns delivering them,

539
00:23:23,830 --> 00:23:25,290
and we still can't keep up.

540
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:26,880
I'm not bragging to you.

541
00:23:29,830 --> 00:23:30,960
Look, another call.

542
00:23:32,470 --> 00:23:33,110
Hello?

543
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,720
Where do you live?

544
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,350
Unit 3, Building 6?

545
00:23:37,830 --> 00:23:40,160
Okay, okay, I'll deliver them right away.

546
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:43,770
Nowadays, everyone is busy

547
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:45,680
with no time to come downstairs.

548
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,240
We should just be diligent,

549
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,560
take phone orders,
and deliver to their doors.

550
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:51,960
So, Sweetie,

551
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:55,000
to do business, you need

552
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:56,920
to open your mind

553
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:58,640
and be flexible like me.

554
00:23:59,350 --> 00:24:00,720
As long as you're capable,

555
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:02,380
you can just make it anywhere.

556
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,070
Dad,

557
00:24:04,160 --> 00:24:05,690
I think I've opened my mind.

558
00:24:08,510 --> 00:24:09,510
What you just said

559
00:24:09,790 --> 00:24:10,830
gives me so much confidence

560
00:24:10,830 --> 00:24:12,360
in opening my online store.

561
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:13,700
Really?

562
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:15,640
When I make money,

563
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:18,000
I'll give you a big red envelope.

564
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,420
What? What did you say?

565
00:24:22,070 --> 00:24:24,330
I said this big bun was really delicious.

566
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:26,980
Eat more if you think it's delicious.

567
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,590
I'm going to deliver buns.

568
00:24:28,590 --> 00:24:30,270
Collecting scrap!

569
00:24:39,730 --> 00:24:40,660
Xuanyu, Doudou.

570
00:24:41,270 --> 00:24:43,160
Alright, you two should take a break.

571
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,820
-Here we go.
-Have some fruit.

572
00:24:45,350 --> 00:24:46,590
The little prince is here.

573
00:24:46,590 --> 00:24:48,590
Come on, my dear Doudou.

574
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:50,930
Would you like some fruit?

575
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:53,010
Look, which one do you want?

576
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:55,460
Which one?

577
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:58,400
Come on, let me get it for you.

578
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,730
Let Mommy get it for you.

579
00:25:01,550 --> 00:25:02,210
Is it yummy?

580
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:03,400
Tell Mommy to have one, too,

581
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:04,000
huh?

582
00:25:04,750 --> 00:25:05,480
Here, honey.

583
00:25:13,270 --> 00:25:13,720
Honey,

584
00:25:14,550 --> 00:25:16,410
can I discuss something with you?

585
00:25:17,070 --> 00:25:17,480
Honey.

586
00:25:19,200 --> 00:25:20,350
Haven't I always been thinking about

587
00:25:20,350 --> 00:25:22,160
